From b7057e5f918b787600f19a76126659decf6bd7d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marie-222 <289302950+marie-222@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:21:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 20/21] desktop-shell: do not ask the RAIL helper for a lock
 surface

In RAIL mode bind_desktop_shell() stores a weston_rdprail_shell resource in
shell->child.desktop_shell. That interface has no events, but unlock() took
the resource for a weston_desktop_shell one and sent prepare_lock_surface
(opcode 1) to it. wl_resource_post_event() then read events[1] of an
interface whose events are NULL and Weston died (SIGSEGV at address 0x20)
at the first mouse move after the idle timeout had locked the shell.

There is no client to ask for a lock surface in RAIL mode: unlock at once,
the same as when the desktop-shell client has gone away.
---
 desktop-shell/shell.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/desktop-shell/shell.c b/desktop-shell/shell.c
index 97f0d4d0..87d381b8 100644
--- a/desktop-shell/shell.c
+++ b/desktop-shell/shell.c
@@ -4582,8 +4582,10 @@ unlock(struct desktop_shell *shell)
 		return;
 	}
 
-	/* If desktop-shell client has gone away, unlock immediately. */
-	if (!shell->child.desktop_shell) {
+	/* If desktop-shell client has gone away, unlock immediately. In RAIL mode
+	 * shell->child.desktop_shell is the weston_rdprail_shell resource of the helper,
+	 * which has no events: there is no client to ask for a lock surface. */
+	if (!shell->child.desktop_shell || shell->rail) {
 		resume_desktop(shell);
 		return;
 	}
